messages:
maya: Heads up — I'm prototyping an autofallback policy for canary rollouts. Need quick sync on ordering & telemetry hooks.

raj: What's the intended priority? model-variant -> region -> capacity? Or prefer regional first to avoid cross-region latency spikes?

maya: Prototype uses model-variant fallback first (cheap + lowest semantic change). If that fails, regional failover to nearby region. Capacity fallback is last: reduce canary weight to 0 then rollback.

sam: How do we define 'fails'? Compatibility (tokenizer/model signature), runtime errors (5xx), and telemetry thresholds. We need explicit checks in the router.

raj: Also suggest multi-metric guards: latency p95, error-rate, avg perplexity delta. A single metric will produce false positives.

ana: Console UX request: a per-rollout 'safe autofallback' toggle and visible decision log (why it switched, what it chose). Customers must be able to opt out.

deploybot: deploybot: canary 2026-03-19T10:14 auto-fallback triggered -> model-variant cpu-quantized at 10:15 due to latency p95 1.7s > 1.5s

sam: We should annotate traces with the decision vector: {metric, threshold, observed}. Also capture GPU util, queue depth, model-load latency.

maya: Draft DSL idea:
```
policy "canary_auto_fallback" {
  priority: ["variant", "region", "capacity"]
  guards: {
    latency_p95: {threshold_ms: 1500, window: 60s}
    error_rate: {threshold_pct: 0.5, window: 60s}
    perplexity_delta: {threshold: 0.1}
  }
  actions: {
    "variant": {fallback_to: "quantized_v2", max_cost_increase_pct: 10}
    "region": {fallback_regions: ["eu-west-1","us-east-1"]}
    "capacity": {reduce_weight_to: 0, notify: ["oncall"]}
  }
}
```

raj: :thumbsup: Two follow-ups — (1) quota enforcement: if fallback raises cost, enforce customer quota to avoid bill shock. (2) Simulate traffic to validate ordering.

ana: UX: show estimated cost delta for each fallback option and require opt-in for > X% cost increase.

sam: Edge case: A/B tests — keep cohort routing immutable; any fallback should preserve cohort mapping or we risk invalidating the test signal.

maya: Action items: 1) add compatibility checks to routing API, 2) push telemetry vector + decision log, 3) console toggle + cost estimate, 4) add quota guard. I'll open an RFC and a staging sim. /cc @sam @raj @ana

raj: Can you include a small perf sim in staging so infra can load-test fallback ordering under contention?

maya: Yep — I'll prototype sim + RFC link: https://rwd.internal/rfcs/1932100000-canary-fallback (draft). Thanks everyone!
